# df(1)

## NAME

df - report file system space usage

## SYNOPSIS

    df [-h|-k] [-i] [file...]

## DESCRIPTION

Prints the size, usage and free space of every mount, with the columns `Filesystem 1K-blocks Used Available Use% Mounted on`. With a file, prints only the mount holding it.

Usage includes file system overhead, so it does not match `du`. The free space of `tmp` is an estimate, as RAM is shared with processes. A mount that cannot report its size shows `-`.

## OPTIONS

- `-h`: sizes in human-readable units (K, M, G)
- `-k`: sizes in KiB (the default)
- `-i`: show entry counts (`Inodes IUsed IFree IUse%`) instead of sizes

## SEE ALSO

du(1), mount(1)
